  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "although-conj",
      "though-conj",
      "even-though-conj"
    ],
    "note": "**Although** and **though** mean the same as conjunctions; **though** is more common in speech, and **although** is a little more formal (*Although the test was hard, I passed*). Only **though** can also come at the end of a sentence (*The test was hard. I passed, though*). **Even though** makes the contrast stronger and is used when the fact is surprising (*Even though he studied all night, he failed*)."
  },
